#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/manage-validation-sets.md:2
msgid "Manage validation sets"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/manage-validation-sets.md:4
msgid ""
"A {ref}`validation sets <explanation-how-snaps-work-validation-sets>` "
"ensures only specific snaps are installed, and optionally, only specific "
"snaps at fixed {ref}`revisions <ref-glossary_revision>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/manage-validation-sets.md:6
msgid ""
"For [Landscape](https://ubuntu.com/landscape)-managed devices, see [How to "
"manage snaps in Landscape with validation sets](https://"
"documentation.ubuntu.com/landscape/how-to-guides/iot-for-devices/manage-"
"snaps-with-validation-sets/) after a validation set has been created."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/manage-validation-sets.md:8
msgid "Create a validation set"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/manage-validation-sets.md:11
msgid ""
"For devices running {ref}`Ubuntu Core <ref-glossary_ubuntu-core>`, a "
"validation set can be declared as part of the [model](https://ubuntu.com/"
"core/docs/reference/assertions/model) definition."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/manage-validation-sets.md:14
msgid ""
"Ensure you have an [Ubuntu One](https://documentation.ubuntu.com/core/"
"tutorials/build-your-first-image/access-ubuntu-one/) and know your "
"*Developer account id*."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/manage-validation-sets.md:16
msgid ""
"The `snapcraft edit-validation-sets` command is used to create a validation "
"set from the command line:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/manage-validation-sets.md:18
msgid "snapcraft edit-validation-sets <account-id> <set-name> <sequence>\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/manage-validation-sets.md:22
msgid ""
"This command requires your developer account id (`<account-id>`), an "
"arbitrary name for the validation set (`<set-name>`), and a sequence number "
"(`<sequence>`). The sequence number starts at 1:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/manage-validation-sets.md:24
msgid ""
"snapcraft edit-validation-sets xSfWKGdLoQBoQx88vIM1MpbFNMq53t1f myset1 1\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/manage-validation-sets.md:28
msgid ""
"An additional `--key-name` argument can be used to specify a key other than "
"the default."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/manage-validation-sets.md:30
msgid "Validation set template"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/manage-validation-sets.md:32
msgid ""
"After running the `edit-validation-sets` command, a text editor will open "
"containing the following template for a validation set assertion that needs "
"to be filled in by the developer issuing the assertion:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/manage-validation-sets.md:34
msgid ""
"account-id: <account-id>\n"
"name: <set-name>\n"
"sequence: <sequence>\n"
"# The revision for this validation set\n"
"# revision: 0\n"
"snaps:\n"
"#  - name: <name>  # The name of the snap.\n"
"#    id:   <id>    # The ID of the snap. Optional, defaults to the current "
"ID for\n"
"                   # the provided name.\n"
"#    presence: [required|optional|invalid]  # Optional, defaults to "
"required.\n"
"#    revision: <n> # The revision of the snap. Optional.\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/manage-validation-sets.md:47
msgid "Template fields"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/manage-validation-sets.md:49
msgid ""
"The template validation set assertion needs to be populated with the details "
"of the snaps you wish to include in the set. These are listed beneath the "
"`snaps:` section, and each snap can use the following fields:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/manage-validation-sets.md:51
msgid ""
"**account-id** (*required*) the brand account associated with this "
"validation set, as retrieved with `snapcraft whoami`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/manage-validation-sets.md:52
msgid "**name** your descriptive name for this validation set."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/manage-validation-sets.md:53
msgid ""
"**sequence** an integer that should be manually incremented with each "
"updated validation set snap or snap revision. If an update fails to apply, "
"snapd can revert only to a previous sequence."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/manage-validation-sets.md:54
msgid ""
"**revision** defaults to 0 if not included. An arbitrary number used to "
"differentiate between different uploaded versions of the validation set."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/manage-validation-sets.md:57
msgid "**snaps:**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/manage-validation-sets.md:58
msgid ""
"**`name`** (*required*):  The name of the snap, as you find on the store or "
"in _snap search_."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/manage-validation-sets.md:60
msgid ""
"**`id`** (*optional*):   The unique snap-id of the snap (see _snap info "
"\\<snap name\\>_ ).  Defaults to the snap-id of the named snap."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/manage-validation-sets.md:63
msgid ""
"**`presence`** (*optional*):  Can be either `required`, `optional` or "
"`invalid`.   `required` snaps need to be installed, `optional` snaps are "
"permitted to be installed and `invalid` snaps explicitly must not be "
"installed.  Defaults to _required_."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/manage-validation-sets.md:67
msgid ""
"**`revision`** (*optional*):  Specifies which revision of the snap needs to "
"be installed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/manage-validation-sets.md:70
msgid ""
"We strongly recommend incrementing the sequence number whenever a validation "
"set used on production devices is modified—especially when updating snap "
"revisions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/manage-validation-sets.md:72
msgid ""
"This enables snapd to revert to the previous validation set if applying the "
"updated assertion fails. The sequence mechanism was introduced to enable "
"safe rollbacks, because reverting to an earlier validation set revision of "
"the same sequence is not supported."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/manage-validation-sets.md:74
msgid "Template example"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/manage-validation-sets.md:76
msgid "A basic validation set template example:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/manage-validation-sets.md:77
msgid ""
"account-id: xSfWKGdLoQBoQx88vIM1MpbFNMq53t1f\n"
"name: myset1\n"
"# revision: 0\n"
"sequence: 1\n"
"snaps:\n"
"  - name: hello-world\n"
"    id: buPKUD3TKqCOgLEjjHx5kSiCpIs5cMuQ\n"
"    presence: required\n"
"  - name: test-snapd-base-bare\n"
"    id: oXC9AkhtCxhlY80KZA3peZzWbnO4xPOT\n"
"    presence: optional\n"
"  - name: bare\n"
"    id: EISPgh06mRh1vordZY9OZ34QHdd7OrdR\n"
"    presence: optional\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/manage-validation-sets.md:94
msgid ""
"We also recommend making a copy of the saved validation set assertion before "
"closing the editor.  Closing the editor will first check the integrity of "
"the assertion before automatically uploading it to the store."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/manage-validation-sets.md:96
msgid ""
"To modify the assertion at a later point, run the same `snapcraft edit-"
"validation-sets` command with the same name but an incremented sequence "
"number and/or revision."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/manage-validation-sets.md:100
msgid ""
"Modifying a validation set without updating the sequence can violate the "
"constraints of an enforced validation set, leading to an invalid state that "
"cannot be automatically recovered. For example, accidentally specifying an "
"approved revision of a snap meant for a different architecture will cause "
"the refresh to fail, leaving the validation set in an invalid state."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/manage-validation-sets.md:103
msgid "<h2 id='heading--listing'>Listing validation sets</h2>\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/manage-validation-sets.md:105
msgid ""
"Use the `snapcraft validation-sets` command to check which validation sets "
"are available in the store:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/manage-validation-sets.md:107
msgid ""
"$ snapcraft validation-sets\n"
"Account-ID                       Name      Sequence  Revision  When\n"
"xSfWKGdLoQBoQx88vIM1MpbFNMq53t1f myset1    1         0         2021-04-08\n"
"xSfWKGdLoQBoQx88vIM1MpbFNMq53t1f testset1  2         0         2021-03-31\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/manage-validation-sets.md:114
msgid ""
"To list only validation-sets with a specific set name, use the additional `--"
"name` argument:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/manage-validation-sets.md:116
msgid ""
"$ snapcraft validation-sets --name myset1\n"
"Account-ID                       Name      Sequence  Revision  When\n"
"xSfWKGdLoQBoQx88vIM1MpbFNMq53t1f myset1    1         0         2021-04-08\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/manage-validation-sets.md:122
msgid ""
"An additional `--sequence` argument can be used to list validation sets with "
"a specific sequence number:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/manage-validation-sets.md:124
msgid ""
"$ snapcraft validation-sets --name myset1 --sequence 1\n"
"Account-ID                       Name      Sequence  Revision  When\n"
"xSfWKGdLoQBoQx88vIM1MpbFNMq53t1f myset1    1         0         2021-04-08\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/manage-validation-sets.md:130
msgid ""
"By default, only the _latest_ validation sets are listed. To list every "
"validation set available, add the `--all` argument."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/manage-validation-sets.md:132
msgid "<h2 id='heading--using'>Monitoring assertion validity</h2>\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/manage-validation-sets.md:134
msgid ""
"The `snap validate --monitor` command is used to enable monitoring of a "
"validation assertion on the system; in this mode the constraints of the "
"assertion are not enforced (e.g. snaps may get automatically refreshed to "
"newer revisions that make the assertion invalid as shown in the next "
"example):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/manage-validation-sets.md:136
msgid "snap validate --monitor xSfWKGdLoQBoQx88vIM1MpbFNMq53t1f/testset1\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/manage-validation-sets.md:140
msgid ""
"The `snap validate` command, with no further arguments, checks whether the "
"`snaps:` rules for all validation set assertions in the store are valid for "
"the system:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/manage-validation-sets.md:142
msgid ""
"$ snap validate\n"
"Validation                                 Mode     Seq  Current    Notes\n"
"xSfWKGdLoQBoQx88vIM1MpbFNMq53t1f/myset1    monitor  1    valid  \n"
"xSfWKGdLoQBoQx88vIM1MpbFNMq53t1f/testset1  monitor  2    invalid\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/manage-validation-sets.md:149
msgid ""
"An assertion is invalid if snaps in the system do not satisfy the "
"constraints of the assertion, such as if required snaps are missing or "
"whether unwanted snaps are present. Multiple validation sets can be used, as "
"shown above, as long as they don't have conflicting constraints and that "
"they can cover different sets of snaps."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/manage-validation-sets.md:151
msgid ""
"A specific validation set can be checked with `snap validate <account id>/"
"<validation set name>`, with an optional sequence point set by adding "
"`=<sequence>` to the validation set name:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/manage-validation-sets.md:153
msgid ""
"$ snap validate xSfWKGdLoQBoQx88vIM1MpbFNMq53t1f/myset1=1\n"
"valid\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/manage-validation-sets.md:158
msgid ""
"A validation set assertion can be _pinned_ by the system administrator at "
"the given sequence number:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/manage-validation-sets.md:160
msgid "snap validate --monitor xSfWKGdLoQBoQx88vIM1MpbFNMq53t1f/testset1=3\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/manage-validation-sets.md:164
msgid ""
"A pinned validation set is kept at the given sequence number, even if "
"there's a higher sequence number in the store. However, the validation will "
"be updated to a newer version if one becomes available with the same "
"sequence number."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/manage-validation-sets.md:166
msgid ""
"Monitor mode validation requires a manual action (`snap validate`, as shown "
"above), but nothing is enforced in the system. Only when _enforce mode_ has "
"been implemented will validation sets have an impact on the system and will "
"prevent installing/removing snaps that violate an assertion's constraints."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/manage-validation-sets.md:168
msgid ""
"Finally, to remove a validation set from the system, use the `--forget` "
"argument:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/manage-validation-sets.md:170
msgid "snap validate --forget xSfWKGdLoQBoQx88vIM1MpbFNMq53t1f/myset1\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/manage-validation-sets.md:174
msgid "<h2 id='heading--enforcing'>Enforcing assertion validity</h2>\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/manage-validation-sets.md:176
msgid ""
"When validation set validity is enforced, snapd will block most operations "
"that would result in snap revisions violating the validation set’s "
"constraints and rendering it invalid. Notably, snapd will not block "
"operations with the `--ignore-validation` flag or local installs by manually "
"downloading and installing a snap."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/manage-validation-sets.md:178
msgid ""
"A validation set can only be enforced if all required snaps are installed, "
"and at the correct revision if specified. This is done by adding the `--"
"enforce` argument to the ‘snap validate’ command:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/manage-validation-sets.md:180
msgid "snap validate --enforce xSfWKGdLoQBoQx88vIM1MpbFNMq53t1f/myset1\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/manage-validation-sets.md:184
msgid ""
"This command will fetch the validation set assertion from the store if not "
"available on the system, but will not refresh assertions, install missing "
"snaps or remove invalid snaps. However, the `--refresh --enforce` arguments "
"can be used to refresh the validation set assertion, install or refresh any "
"snaps and revisions required for the assertion to become valid. Note that, "
"if the assertion requires snaps to be removed, the `--refresh --enforce` "
"request will not remove them and will instead quit without making any "
"changes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/manage-validation-sets.md:186
msgid ""
"snap validate --refresh --enforce xSfWKGdLoQBoQx88vIM1MpbFNMq53t1f/myset1\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/manage-validation-sets.md:190
msgid ""
"After enforcement is enabled, snapd ensures the consistency of the enforced "
"validation sets, and the snaps they reference, during install (only when "
"installing through the store), refresh and remove operations."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/manage-validation-sets.md:192
msgid ""
"During auto-refreshes or manual refreshes, enforced validation set "
"assertions on the system may be updated to a newer revision."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/manage-validation-sets.md:194
msgid ""
"If a validation set assertion is not pinned to a specific sequence, the "
"system will move to the latest sequence available in the store, provided "
"that the installed snaps, including any newer revisions available in store, "
"satisfy its constraints."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/manage-validation-sets.md:196
msgid ""
"However, if the assertion is pinned to a specific sequence, or if a newer "
"revision of the same sequence is available, the system will move to that "
"revision without re-evaluating whether its constraints are still satisfied. "
"This can cause the validation set to become invalid without warning."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/manage-validation-sets.md:198
msgid ""
"To ensure safe rollbacks and consistent behavior, always increment the "
"sequence number when creating a new revision of a validation set used in "
"production."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/manage-validation-sets.md:200
msgid ""
"In this way, the `snapcraft edit-validation-sets` command can be used to "
"control the updates of multiple snaps at the same time."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/manage-validation-sets.md:202
msgid ""
"For brief periods during multi-snap updates, different snap revisions, from "
"previous and incoming validation set sequence points, can co-exist. "
"Validation set enforcement is not intended to deal with any breaking hard "
"version dependencies during transitions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/manage-validation-sets.md:204
msgid ""
"As with monitor mode, enforcing can be disabled for select validation sets "
"with the ‘snap validate --forget’ command."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/manage-snaps/manage-validation-sets.md:206
msgid ""
"When using `snap install` and `snap refresh`, the `--ignore-validation` flag "
"can be added to bypass validation set enforcement for the snaps affected. "
"Doing so will ignore the validation of the given snap, and for subsequent "
"refresh operations. This may result in the validation set becoming _invalid_ "
"in `snap validate` output. Local snap installation will always bypass "
"validation set enforcement since the purposeful act of installing a specific "
"snap already indicates that a user is acting intentionally."
msgstr ""
